mes and a tmpfs. Coverage ledger not recorded, so left unknown.'\nA flag B01 --evidence app/tools/__init__.py:69 --note 'Extractor role name mismatch falls back to the procurement tool list.'\nA item B01 --rating gap --confidence high --summary 'The extractor sub-agent silently gets the full procurement tool list, and ERP operations are allowed by prefix, not by name.' --next 'Fail closed on unknown roles, fix the extractor role name, and replace prefix matching in erp_call with an exact operation allowlist.' --violates \"Enforce a role-based allowlist, and check that an unlisted tool can't be called\"\nA check B02.1 --met unknown --note 'Only ServiceAccount (serviceaccount.yaml) is in the repo. No IAM, Role or RoleBinding for the agent; cloud and STS policy live outside.'\nA check B02.2 --met no --evidence app/tools/memory.py:44 --quote 'business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant' --note 'memory_read takes the tenant from a model-supplied argument (schema allows business_unit), so the model can read another unit notes. ERP and documents use ident.tenant correctly (erp.py:26, documents.py:27).'\nA check B02.3 --met unknown --evidence app/identity.py:106 --note 'Tokens are requested with an audience (identity.py:106) but ERP gateway, payments and Slack proxy validation is outside this repo.'\nA check B02.4 --met unknown --note 'identity.py:104-110 exchanges the workload token with the delegated subject as actor_token, and user tokens are not forwarded. STS verification of the actor_token is outside this repo.'\nA flag B02 --evidence app/tools/memory.py:44 --note 'Model-controlled business_unit in memory_read crosses the tenant boundary.'\nA flag B02 --evidence config/policy.yaml:23 --note 'operation_scopes grants write scopes (erp.vendor.write, erp.invoice.write) to operations reachable through the generic erp_call tool.'\nA item B02 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary 'Tenant scope in memory_read is chosen by the model, and write scopes are mintable through the generic erp_call tool.' --next 'Always use ident.tenant in memory_read, and request write scopes only through gated named tools.' --violates 'Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries'\nA check B03.1 --met unknown --note 'Credentials come from a projected SA token exchanged at the STS (identity.py:91-117, deployment.yaml:104-107). No static API key was found, but no coverage ledger was recorded.'\nA check B03.2 --met unknown --evidence deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:107 --note 'Workload token is 600s (deployment.yaml:107). Access token lifetime comes from STS expires_in (identity.py:115), set outside this repo. No rotation config in repo.'\nA check B03.3 --met unknown --note 'Searched app, config, deploy, Dockerfile, release, migrations for key-like literals; none found. Secrets are mounted from Kubernetes Secrets. No coverage ledger recorded.'\nA check B03.4 --met unknown --evidence app/tools/payments.py:32 --quote '\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",' --note 'Plain bearer tokens are used. No holder binding (mTLS/DPoP) is configured, and whether the services support it is not stated.'\nA item B03 --rating needs_evidence --confidence low --summary 'Credentials look short-lived and federated, but lifetimes and holder binding cannot be confirmed from this repo.' --next 'Provide STS token lifetime and rotation config, and state whether services support DPoP or mTLS.'\nA check B04.1 --met unknown --note 'No disable/revoke path for the agent identity in the repo. Identity is separate from the user (identity.py:4-6), and killswitch.py only blocks new runs.'\nA check B04.2 --met unknown --note 'Revocation enforcement would be at STS or gateway, outside this repo.'\nA check B04.3 --met no --evidence app/identity.py:97 --quote 'if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():' --note 'No revocation limit is stated anywhere in the repo. Tokens are cached until expiry and no introspection, deny list or CAEP is used.